<% genes = @manifest["genes"] %>
<% baseline = @clustering && @clustering["silhouette_baseline"] %>
Hello,

Your RNA-seq analysis (Job #<%= @job.job_number %>) is complete.

Analysis: <%= @question %>

Results
- Samples analyzed: <%= number_with_delimiter(@manifest["samples"]["in_model"]) %>
- Genes tested: <%= number_with_delimiter(genes["tested"]) %> of <%= number_with_delimiter(genes["in_input"]) %>
- Significant genes: <%= number_with_delimiter(genes["significant"]) %><% unless genes["significant_up"].nil? %> (<%= number_with_delimiter(genes["significant_up"]) %> higher and <%= number_with_delimiter(genes["significant_down"]) %> lower in <%= @manifest.dig("contrast", "test_level") %>)<% end %>
<% if @clustering %>
- Gene clusters: <%= @clustering["clusters"] %> (silhouette <%= format("%.2f", @clustering["silhouette"]) %>)
<% end %>
<% if baseline %>
- Silhouette reliability check: actual <%= format("%.2f", baseline["actual"]) %>, shuffled baseline <%= format("%.2f", baseline["shuffled_mean"]) %>, difference <%= format("%+.2f", baseline["difference"]) %> (near 0 would mean no better than random patterns)
<% end %>

Statistical method: <%= @method %>

Attached: <%= @file_names.join(", ") %>
<% if @warnings.present? %>

Please note
<% @warnings.each do |warning| %>
- <%= warning[:analysis] %>: <%= warning[:message] %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

The ZIP contains your results and plots. See README.txt for file descriptions, analysis settings, and statistical methods. Related papers are available on MicroNet’s Resources page.

Best,
